hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16700","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Qari, from his father, from his grandfather Amr ibn al-Qari that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and left Sad ill when he went out to Hunayn. When he came from Jiranah performing Umrah, he entered upon him while he was pained, overcome. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth, and I am inherited as kalalah; shall I bequeath all my wealth or give it in charity. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath two-thirds. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath half. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath a third. He said: Yes, and that is much. He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I die in the abode from which I emigrated. He said: I hope Allah will raise you, harming peoples through you and benefiting others through you. O Amr ibn al-Qari, if Sad dies after me, then here bury him toward the road of Madinah. And he gestured with his hand thus."
